            <div class="lead" style="font-size:19px;line-height:1.6;margin-bottom:32px;color:#bbb;">
              Every engagement at Apex Marketings runs through the same four-stage process: <strong>Discovery → Strategy → Launch → Optimization</strong>. This page explains what each stage produces, what we need from you, and how long it takes. Procurement teams: this is the document to share with stakeholders.
            </div>
            <style>article a {color:rgb(20,120,190);text-decoration:underline;} article h2 {margin-top:48px;} article h3 {margin-top:32px;}</style>
            <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">Stage 1 — Discovery (1-2 weeks)</h2>
              <p>A paid sprint (USD 500-2,000 depending on scope) that produces a written marketing audit, KPI plan, and 90-day action plan. Output is yours regardless of whether you proceed.</p>
              <p><strong>What you do:</strong> share access to existing analytics, ad accounts (read-only), and current marketing assets. Typical commitment: 3-5 hours across 2 calls.</p>
              <p><strong>What we do:</strong> audit current performance, interview key stakeholders, analyze competitors, identify quick wins, draft KPI targets, propose channel mix and budget allocation.</p>
              <p><strong>You receive:</strong> (a) written audit document, (b) competitor benchmark report, (c) channel-mix recommendation, (d) 90-day action plan with milestones, (e) fixed-fee or retainer quote, (f) named strategist + team.</p>
              <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">Stage 2 — Strategy & Setup (1-3 weeks)</h2>
              <p>After contract signing, we build the campaign infrastructure: tracking, landing pages, ad creative, content templates, email flows. This is the foundation work that makes Stage 3 productive.</p>
              <p><strong>Typical Stage 2 deliverables:</strong></p>
              <ul style="line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;margin:20px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom:10px;">Analytics setup: GA4, Meta Pixel, GTM, server-side tracking, custom dashboards</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;">Ad accounts setup: Google Ads, Meta Business Manager, with proper conversion tracking</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;">Landing pages: 2-4 dedicated landing pages per campaign goal</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;">Initial creative: ad copy, ad creative (image / video), email templates</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;">Content briefs: 2-3 cornerstone SEO articles outlined and ready to write</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;">Reporting: dashboard URLs, weekly status format, KPI definitions</li></ul>
              <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">Stage 3 — Launch & Execution (ongoing)</h2>
              <p>Campaigns go live. We monitor daily for the first 14 days to catch and fix issues fast. After that, we run weekly optimization cycles.</p>
              <ul style="line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;margin:20px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Day 1-14:</strong> intensive monitoring — daily check-ins, immediate fixes</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Day 15-60:</strong> weekly optimization — kill underperformers, double down on winners</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Day 60+:</strong> bi-weekly optimization rhythm with monthly strategic reviews</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Continuous:</strong> creative refresh every 14-30 days, A/B tests on landing pages, content cadence</li></ul>
              <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">Stage 4 — Optimization & Scale (Month 3 onwards)</h2>
              <p>Once campaigns are stable and KPIs are tracking, we shift to compounding gains: scaling winning channels, expanding to new ones, refining attribution, raising LTV through retention loops.</p>
              <p><strong>Typical month 3+ activities:</strong></p>
              <ul style="line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;margin:20px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom:10px;">Scale winning ad creative + audiences</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;">Launch retention loops (email, SMS, retargeting)</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;">Add second/third paid channel once primary is profitable</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;">Build content engine for compound SEO growth</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;">Refine attribution model (server-side tracking, view-through analysis)</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;">Quarterly business review with strategic roadmap update</li></ul>
              <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">What you can expect from us</h2>
              <ul style="line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;margin:20px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Written communication:</strong> every decision, status update, and trade-off in writing</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>No surprise costs:</strong> Change Orders for any scope shifts before doing the work</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Single point of contact:</strong> one strategist owns your account end-to-end</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Direct access to specialists:</strong> not just the PM — talk to the people running your ads</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Your accounts stay yours:</strong> we never own the ad accounts; you control credentials</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Honest risk surfacing:</strong> if something is going wrong, we tell you immediately</li></ul>
              <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">What we ask of you</h2>
              <ul style="line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;margin:20px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Decision turnaround within 48 business hours</strong> — fast clients = fast projects</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>One person with approval authority</strong> for scope and budget</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Access to subject experts</strong> on your team when we need product / industry knowledge</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Honest scope</strong> — tell us the constraints you can't move on</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Timely payments</strong> — healthy cash flow protects execution quality</li></ul>
            <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4 mt-5">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
              <h3 class="cs-font_24 mt-4 mb-2">Can we skip Discovery?</h3><p>Only for very small projects (under USD 1,500). For everything else, skipping Discovery is the #1 reason marketing engagements fail.</p>
              <h3 class="cs-font_24 mt-4 mb-2">What if we need to change scope mid-engagement?</h3><p>Change Order: documented impact, new timeline, new budget, your approval. Most engagements have 1-3 Change Orders; that's normal.</p>
              <h3 class="cs-font_24 mt-4 mb-2">How do you handle disagreements?</h3><p>We surface disagreement explicitly with 2-3 paths forward and our recommendation. If unresolved, the engagement contract includes a step-up procedure.</p>
              <h3 class="cs-font_24 mt-4 mb-2">Can we visit your office?</h3><p>Yes. Our Rawalpindi office welcomes client visits. Most Pakistani clients visit during kickoff. International clients usually meet via video.</p>
              <h3 class="cs-font_24 mt-4 mb-2">What happens at the end of the engagement?</h3><p>Handover documentation, account credential transfer (your accounts stay yours), 30-day support window. Many clients renew; that's fine. Some take it in-house; that's also fine — we don't hold you hostage.</p>
